{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q167525","formula":"Mg₆Al₂(CO₃)(OH)₁₆*4H₂O","hill":"CH24Al2Mg6O23","elements":["H","C","O","Mg","Al"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":24.0,"O":23.0,"Al":2.0,"Mg":6.0},"names":{"en":"Hydrotalcite","uk":"Гідроталькіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hydrotalcite, or formerly also völknerite, is a layered double hydroxide (LDH) of general formula Mg6Al2CO3(OH)16·4H2O, whose name is derived from its resemblance with talc and its high water content. Multiple structures containing loosely bound carbonate (CO2−3) ions exist. The easily exchangeable carbonates enable applications of the mineral in wastewater treatment and the immobilisation of radioactive waste after nuclear fuel reprocessing.","uk":"Гідроталькіт (рос. гідроталькіт; англ. hydrotalcite; нім."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q167525","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrotalcite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D1%96%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BA%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hydrotalcite-200667.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q3927919","formula":"Mg₄Al₂(OH)₁₂(CO₃)·3H₂O","names":{"en":"Quintinite"},"elements":["H","C","O","Mg","Al"],"fame":9,"kind":null},{"id":"Q4733653","formula":"CH₁₁AlMg₃O₁₂","names":{"en":"Almagate dihydrate"},"elements":["H","C","O","Mg","Al"],"fame":6,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q2738075","formula":"Mg₆Cr₂CO₃(OH)₁₆·4H₂O","names":{"en":"Stichtite","uk":"Стихтит"},"elements":["H","C